rule of navigation
like aunts trying to climb a tree, jumping or flying around the branches is not possible, we should use the long way, like wise if we want to access adirectory the same level as another directory we are in, we should first move back to their parent directory and only after the we can access the directory we want, we can move from the directory to the parent directory and then to the directory we want or simply use ../ + the directory name we want to access, .. is used to move back from a diretory and / to enteranother directory
ls ..---to see the list of the directories and the files of the parent directory while being in one of the children
ls ../ + directory--gives the lists of the files inside a directory while being in another directory
cd ../.. --from child to another child, then even go up to another child or go into root directory

